TAG
A tag is a name attached to one commit. A branch name is a pointer that moves forward with every new commit. A tag points at one commit until someone deliberately replaces it. Teams keep release tags fixed by convention, so they identify the exact commit that shipped as version 1.0.

Two kinds of tags
A lightweight tag is just the name and the commit hash, nothing else: git tag v0.1.
An annotated tag is a full object with its own message, tagger, and date. You create it with -a and -m:

Tagging older commit  - git tag -a v1.0 -m "First production release" 4a7d1c2

